Summary of modifications made by Kagayoi:

  - Retargeted the plugin from the OpenAI Codex CLI to xAI's Grok Build CLI.
  - Replaced the Codex app-server JSON-RPC transport with an Agent Client
    Protocol (ACP) client that speaks to `grok agent stdio`, including
    handling of agent-to-client requests (permission prompts and file I/O)
    that the Codex protocol did not have.
  - Replaced Codex's built-in `review/start` reviewer with a prompt-driven,
    schema-constrained review that enforces read-only access through an
    allowlist applied to the agent's permission requests.
  - Removed the `/codex:transfer` command and its supporting code, because
    Grok Build has no equivalent of Codex's external-agent session import.
  - Renamed the plugin, its commands, skills, and configuration from the
    `codex` namespace to the `grok` namespace.

